@lisihao/dsh-solar-bench README · Using it in the app：- **基准库 / Library**: one sub-tab per category: Agents & tool calling, Programming, General knowledge & reasoning, Mathematics & logic, Multimodal & long context, Human preference & arenas, Long-horizon tasks, Recursive self-improvement, AI for Science, and Harness comparison. Each benchmark card shows what it measures, its source, paper and license, the item count, any measurement caveat, its protocol, and its latest result. A benchmark that cannot run here says why (Docker, gated dataset, images, multi-turn user simulation, expert grading, no license…).
- **运行记录 / Run records**: every experiment, newest first, filtered by category (benchmarks not in the catalog fall under 其他 / Other); the running experiment shows its count and spend, and **查看分析** opens one experiment's comparisons, variants, time split, cost front and per-item matrix.
- **对照分析 / Comparisons**: a scoreboard of benchmarks (rows, grouped by category) × compositions (columns: the baseline under each driver, then each plugin), each cell the latest experiment's pass rate ×100 (MT-Bench: mean score ×100). Bold is the best within the row's latest experiment; cells from

@lisihao/dsh-solar-bench README · Container benchmarks (Harbor)：- **Needs on this computer**: a running Docker (or OrbStack) and Harbor 0.25.0 (`uv tool install harbor==0.25.0`). Neither arrives with the plugin. The card is startable only when `docker info` answers and `harbor --version` prints 0.25.0 (searched on `PATH`, Homebrew, `~/.local/bin` and OrbStack); otherwise it names what is missing. Start probes again.
- **A trial**: the plugin runs `harbor run -p <task> --agent solar_bench_dsh_agent:DshAgent` with this package's `harbor/` directory on `PYTHONPATH`. The agent installs Node 22 and `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.1-rc.2` in the task container, uses dsh's built-in `headless` profile (`dsh-base` + `dsh-headless`), installs the plugin under test into it from the source profile's own dependency spec (a local tarball is uploaded; npm and git specs install with network during setup; a linked directory is refused), applies the driver and web-off patches, and runs one turn with the task's instruction. Harbor's verifier grades it; the reward in [0, 1] is the score, and 0.6 (RSI-Exam's reference line) or more counts as a pass.
